  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Antes que», «até que», «sem que»",
     "texto": [
      "**Antes que** (before), **até que** (until) and **sem que** (without) usually take the subjunctive for an action not yet done: **Antes que saias, fecha a porta** (before you leave, close the door), **Até que chegues** (until you arrive). The subject can be the same or different."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Antes de» + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "With **antes de**, the infinitive can stay uninflected when the subject is clear from context: **Antes de sair, vou fechar a porta** (before leaving, I'll close the door). If the subject of the subordinate clause is expressed or it's important to identify it, it can be inflected: **Antes de saíres, vou fechar a porta** (before you leave, I'll close the door).",
      "**Saíres** is the personal infinitive of «tu»; it is not a subjunctive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
